            hook: "Home-court rule: one served defendant at home is enough to block a diversity-only removal.",
            stem: "A citizen of State A sued a contractor, a citizen of State B, and a supplier, a citizen of State C, in a State B state court for $250,000 in damages for negligence under State B law arising from the collapse of a loading dock. Both defendants were served on May 3. On May 28, they filed a joint notice of removal in the federal district court for the district embracing the state court. On June 10, the plaintiff moved to remand the case to state court.",
